{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A5LwDcNoACB3TCTAT4yxJu","type":"tool_result","content":"854:[Omitted long matching line]\n858:Why two? Footprint. A vanilla Fluentd instance \"runs on 30-40MB of memory\" [source: fluentd-architecture-2026-08-31] — trivial on a server, less trivial multiplied across every node in a large fleet, and genuinely limiting on constrained hardware. Fluent Bit is the lightweight answer. Both \"are commonly deployed on Kubernetes as node-level logging agents (DaemonSets) that collect container logs from each node and forward them to a backend\" [source: fluent-bit-overview-2026-08-23].\n860:Fluent Bit's pipeline has six stages, in order [source: fluent-bit-overview-2026-08-23]:\n862:| Stage | What it does |\n868:| **Router** | Routes data through filters and on to one or more destinations, using tags and matching rules |\n869:| **Output** | Plugins define destinations — remote services, local filesystems, standard interfaces |\n1381:- **C** inverts them. Fluentd is the parent and heavier — \"30-40MB of memory\" for a vanilla instance [source: fluentd-architecture-2026-08-31]."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95a83325-4699-403f-9a95-418f171c160c","uuid":"aa9511d3-2911-4181-a16b-3e580b6d9d5c","timestamp":"2026-08-31T21:19:55.218Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"854:[Omitted long matching line]\n858:Why two? Footprint. A vanilla Fluentd instance \"runs on 30-40MB of memory\" [source: fluentd-architecture-2026-08-31] — trivial on a server, less trivial multiplied across every node in a large fleet, and genuinely limiting on constrained hardware. Fluent Bit is the lightweight answer. Both \"are commonly deployed on Kubernetes as node-level logging agents (DaemonSets) that collect container logs from each node and forward them to a backend\" [source: fluent-bit-overview-2026-08-23].\n860:Fluent Bit's pipeline has six stages, in order [source: fluent-bit-overview-2026-08-23]:\n862:| Stage | What it does |\n868:| **Router** | Routes data through filters and on to one or more destinations, using tags and matching rules |\n869:| **Output** | Plugins define destinations — remote services, local filesystems, standard interfaces |\n1381:- **C** inverts them. Fluentd is the parent and heavier — \"30-40MB of memory\" for a vanilla instance [source: fluentd-architecture-2026-08-31].","numLines":7,"totalLines":7}}
